## ✅ Vite config fixed

I cleaned up the proxy config so local development uses the Laravel API on localhost:

```ts
import { defineConfig } from 'vite'
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'

// https://vite.dev/config/
export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  server: {
    port: 5173,
    proxy: {
      '/api': {
        target: 'http://localhost:8741',
        changeOrigin: true,
        secure: false,
      },
    },
  },
})
```

This keeps:
- React on port `5173`
- Laravel API on `http://localhost:8741`
- frontend fetches like `/api/register` working during local development

If you want, I can next check the actual app behavior with the dev server and make sure the login/register flow works through this proxy.

